{"version":3,"kind":"Notebook","sha256":"98183443699060a30d2388003e2d98e9a206dac684669f8cb84fec0f9dd9113e","slug":"crocodash.projects.ocean-only","location":"/crocodash/projects/ocean_only.ipynb","dependencies":[],"frontmatter":{"title":"Project: Ocean Only Configuration - The Bare Minimum","content_includes_title":false,"kernelspec":{"name":"python3","display_name":"CrocoDash","language":"python"},"github":"https://github.com/CROCODILE-CESM/CrocoGallery","numbering":{"title":{"offset":2}},"source_url":"https://github.com/CROCODILE-CESM/CrocoGallery/blob/main/crocodash/projects/ocean_only.ipynb","edit_url":"https://github.com/CROCODILE-CESM/CrocoGallery/edit/main/crocodash/projects/ocean_only.ipynb","exports":[{"format":"ipynb","filename":"ocean_only.ipynb","url":"/CrocoGallery/latest/build/ocean_only-a4cdff55bbf225d3ab63a74263f99e22.ipynb"}]},"widgets":{},"mdast":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-content","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"This project is all about how we create the most basic ocean_only domain to shake things out and get spinning as fast as possible. This is one way of testing everything before we get into our research questions.","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"h4usBUVowl"}],"key":"jfNX8Co0jD"}],"identifier":"84b4b4ad","html_id":"84b4b4ad","key":"R2hNBsFNMA"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-content","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Download this project by either:","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"t6jGGs27uV"}],"key":"ASVa1hIkEA"},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"spread":false,"position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":4,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Running the CrocoDash CLI command: ","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"v5uXBaV3YD"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"crocodash template --output ocean_only_case.ipynb --machine glade --notebook crocodash.projects.ocean_only","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"iQ2EMSrO7i"},{"type":"text","value":", then filling in the paths it leaves as placeholders","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"BnxYuWjXhK"}],"key":"HPyokJ8wYp"}],"key":"uhdgm4UaCw"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":4,"column":1},"end":{"line":4,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Copying the file from your CrocoDash checkout: ","position":{"start":{"line":4,"column":1},"end":{"line":4,"column":1}},"key":"sY3e3GCLOW"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gallery/crocodash/projects/ocean_only.ipynb","position":{"start":{"line":4,"column":1},"end":{"line":4,"column":1}},"key":"fGstTXj37Z"}],"key":"NGyBoycqCX"}],"key":"lHHkxlz4t1"}],"key":"Ee94aRGp2a"}],"identifier":"d75d080e","html_id":"d75d080e","key":"EvdmhXAgKH"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-content","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Grid Generation","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"il3n02YjLO"}],"identifier":"grid-generation","label":"Grid Generation","html_id":"grid-generation","implicit":true,"key":"pSBiLXWx8I"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The first thing we are going to do is think about how to get a domain. Scaling data is available online, but a 100x100 point domain is relatively quick. If we provide ~40 cores for the ocean, it’ll run within a few minutes.","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"x7Z82i8NbL"}],"key":"o2n0y4xRav"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":5,"column":1},"end":{"line":5,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"We’ll pick a 100x100 point horizontal grid and a standard vertical grid.","position":{"start":{"line":5,"column":1},"end":{"line":5,"column":1}},"key":"dDmPGnBAGX"}],"key":"tkiDeDAijU"}],"identifier":"e0fc8055","html_id":"e0fc8055","key":"uyB92RyLfF"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-code","children":[{"type":"code","lang":"python","executable":true,"value":"from CrocoDash.grid import Grid\nfrom CrocoDash.vgrid import VGrid\n\ngrid = Grid(\n  resolution = 0.05, # in degrees\n  xstart = 278.0, # min longitude in [0, 360]\n  lenx = 5.0, # longitude extent in degrees\n  ystart = 7.0, # min latitude in [-90, 90]\n  leny = 5.0, # latitude extent in degrees\n  name = \"basic_grid\",\n)\n\n\nvgrid  = VGrid.hyperbolic(\n    nk = 75, # number of vertical levels\n    depth = 2000,\n    ratio=20.0 # target ratio of top to bottom layer thicknesses\n)","key":"SCV1aJlwEf"},{"type":"outputs","id":"yXU2er81xIGclZZ4fEDY5","children":[],"key":"uUakCkHrAz"}],"identifier":"0325b73d","html_id":"0325b73d","key":"PJcaPRS6NS"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-content","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Now that we have our horizontal and vertical grids, we need to setup our bathymetry. Normally, we’d use the ","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"YX6xtCwB1e"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Topo.set_from_dataset","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"ghO9vZ0b4H"},{"type":"text","value":" function to go from a bathymetry dataset to grid bathymetry. However, as a first step we’ll skip the dataset entirely and use an idealized bathymetry. ","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"I3NRUTG7fk"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Topo","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"isIyBFFwzM"},{"type":"text","value":" provides helpers mirroring MOM6’s built-in TOPO_CONFIG options, such as ","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"v7Ks5TMIk0"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"spoon","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"GJihpYjKRM"},{"type":"text","value":", the analytic basin shape used in MOM6’s idealized double gyre case.","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"VQgF8hh1L9"}],"key":"OKrdpUWagB"}],"identifier":"35338f50","html_id":"35338f50","key":"bLh4jXXoC5"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-code","children":[{"type":"code","lang":"python","executable":true,"value":"from CrocoDash.topo import Topo\n\ntopo = Topo(\n    grid = grid,\n    min_depth = 9.5, # in meters\n)\n\ntopo.set_spoon(max_depth = 2000, dedge = 200)\n\ntopo.depth.plot()","key":"NFoG6B0kIZ"},{"type":"outputs","id":"vMI5_NX2T3XCnyrIhjBxE","children":[],"key":"f3HsoHWMZJ"}],"identifier":"664779d2","html_id":"664779d2","key":"v4p1eBjGKo"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-content","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Great! So I’m going to create my case now, and this step will hardly ever change!","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"a4RCl0jckJ"}],"key":"sVgNUbodsV"}],"identifier":"4e386f52","html_id":"4e386f52","key":"mMP6HkweRI"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-code","children":[{"type":"code","lang":"python","executable":true,"value":"from pathlib import Path\nfrom CrocoDash.case import Case\n\n# CESM case (experiment) name\ncasename = \"basic_ocean\"\n\n# CESM source root (Update this path accordingly!!!)\ncesmroot =\"<CESM>\"\n\n# Place where all your input files go \ninputdir = Path(\"<inputdir>\") / casename\n    \n# CESM case directory\ncaseroot = Path(\"<casedir>\") / casename\n\n\ncase = Case(\n    cesmroot = cesmroot,\n    caseroot = caseroot,\n    inputdir = inputdir,\n    ocn_grid = grid,\n    ocn_vgrid = vgrid,\n    ocn_topo = topo,\n    project = \"<PROJECT>\", # Update this with your project code\n    job_queue = \"<JOB_QUEUE>\", # PBS queue the run is submitted to\n    job_wallclock_time = \"<WALLCLOCK_1H>\", # hh:mm:ss walltime requested for the run\n    override = True,\n    machine = \"derecho\",\n    compset = \"CR_JRA\"\n)","key":"RYipUE4yiM"},{"type":"outputs","id":"NVXh2UEp3hroIZvT1XMVA","children":[],"key":"prOMvMnVvF"}],"identifier":"ca45d4f1","html_id":"ca45d4f1","key":"z4KOGUQEW0"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-content","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Now, the last step is to generate forcings, which is done as a two step configure and process. Since it can take a long time to get raw data from outside sources, we’re going to use a fake data generator that comes with CrocoDash.","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"Yd3vtlcnN3"}],"key":"A8jBvtxQn4"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"I also think we can run for 60 days. That doesn’t sound too bad.","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"ER3Ddjn6lc"}],"key":"qcTRKWeXql"}],"identifier":"44b97111","html_id":"44b97111","key":"qfjgTHUpPM"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-code","children":[{"type":"code","lang":"python","executable":true,"value":"case.configure_forcings(\n    date_range = [\"2019-01-01 00:00:00\", \"2019-03-03 00:00:00\"],\n    product_name=\"reference_ocean\",\n    function_name=\"get_reference_ocean_data\"\n)\n","key":"PX3lWhShPl"},{"type":"outputs","id":"947vWJt0Kfcy-zUcYZCL5","children":[],"key":"yJGOWASsx8"}],"identifier":"7ff41626","html_id":"7ff41626","key":"gW3mLN2uw7"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-code","children":[{"type":"code","lang":"python","executable":true,"value":"case.process_forcings()\n","key":"fwdHcQqzy2"},{"type":"outputs","id":"InhhAeoi7PCCMiCIEBDFG","children":[],"key":"EdXCSMlO6N"}],"identifier":"890857d3","html_id":"890857d3","key":"YjD6u453XH"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-content","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cool! Once this is done, we have to ","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"ZSZrUiodXu"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"./case.build","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"mxnUPczh6H"},{"type":"text","value":" and ","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"OnLcbZWk6A"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"./case.submit","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"dfaRblBXs9"},{"type":"text","value":" in our case directory. Before that though, here’s some things I’d ","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"Cd4iXxhnac"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"xmlchange","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"ezgfyh3ANX"},{"type":"text","value":" to make the domain run faster.","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"uuF3sbrcQw"}],"key":"g2zYXr6rfY"},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"spread":false,"position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":8,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"I’d set the ","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"QpVC4YwpwS"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"NTASKS = 10","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"am45WiP6Y9"},{"type":"text","value":", which sets every component to 10 cores, and makes the data atmosphere regridding very fast. (All components share these 10 cores)","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"AUFGAXndOx"}],"key":"imv3ojKYYy"}],"key":"RAsQtAMlQu"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":4,"column":1},"end":{"line":4,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"I’d set the ","position":{"start":{"line":4,"column":1},"end":{"line":4,"column":1}},"key":"bSO2irBTSa"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"NTASKS_OCN = 40","position":{"start":{"line":4,"column":1},"end":{"line":4,"column":1}},"key":"GzKZqynAEU"},{"type":"text","value":" because of the scaling data we saw: ","position":{"start":{"line":4,"column":1},"end":{"line":4,"column":1}},"key":"KbjA9xEGZ3"},{"type":"link","url":"https://crocodile-cesm.github.io/SeaSloth/mom6_scaling.html","position":{"start":{"line":4,"column":1},"end":{"line":4,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"https://​crocodile​-cesm​.github​.io​/SeaSloth​/mom6​_scaling​.html","position":{"start":{"line":4,"column":1},"end":{"line":4,"column":1}},"key":"G4kJwSRhsB"}],"urlSource":"https://crocodile-cesm.github.io/SeaSloth/mom6_scaling.html","key":"QCOKWEbcui"}],"key":"Lyf3wNZ7jP"}],"key":"qO4SKChisx"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":5,"column":1},"end":{"line":5,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"I’d set the ","position":{"start":{"line":5,"column":1},"end":{"line":5,"column":1}},"key":"LzqnEN0Jru"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ROOTPE = 0","position":{"start":{"line":5,"column":1},"end":{"line":5,"column":1}},"key":"jZlqEBQdDg"},{"type":"text","value":", which ensures that all components share the same cores. If I set ROOTPE_OCN=10, it would skip the first 10 cores and run on the next 40 cores.","position":{"start":{"line":5,"column":1},"end":{"line":5,"column":1}},"key":"DRjpMbrTpA"}],"key":"OhO096JE4g"}],"key":"kU68xUEolI"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":6,"column":1},"end":{"line":8,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"I’d set the ","position":{"start":{"line":6,"column":1},"end":{"line":6,"column":1}},"key":"VAVxSs9k8L"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"JOB_WALLCLOCK_TIME = 00:30:00 --subgroup case.run","position":{"start":{"line":6,"column":1},"end":{"line":6,"column":1}},"key":"vsXwvvWaOr"},{"type":"text","value":", which ensures the queue picks up our job realllly fast.","position":{"start":{"line":6,"column":1},"end":{"line":6,"column":1}},"key":"HrM2PsL7Ny"}],"key":"jh58fZngBl"}],"key":"qRi70ULbcI"}],"key":"q1dydM3fbN"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":9,"column":1},"end":{"line":9,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"And there we go! A fake running ocean model! Isn’t that awesome!","position":{"start":{"line":9,"column":1},"end":{"line":9,"column":1}},"key":"BY3V8XZZc3"}],"key":"od6YsW0dJ1"}],"identifier":"6fa10400","html_id":"6fa10400","key":"yXJJ1U9sBL"}],"key":"T4PzyoBaAg"},"references":{"cite":{"order":[],"data":{}}},"footer":{"navigation":{"prev":{"title":"CROCODILE 2026 Workshop Projects","short_title":"Projects","url":"/crocodash/projects","group":"Use Cases"},"next":{"title":"Project: CICE Configuration - Ayy, It’s Chilly!","url":"/crocodash/projects/cice","group":"Use Cases"}}},"domain":"http://localhost:3000"}